WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.700
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.400
make sure you're in a well-lit
room and sit far away from the TV!

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.010
It's no use. I can't find anything.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.600
I'm so hungry, I'm about to pass out...

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.020
Are you sure they're here, Jasmine?

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.980
They must be here.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.300
This is a marbleberry tree, after all.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.000
This is so strange, there's no fruit here at all.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.500
Here they are!

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.800
So this is our lunch today?

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.200
It can't be helped. Let's split
them between us and eat.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.400
Are we really going to split
<i>this</i> between the three of us?

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.100
No, make that five.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.000
Hey!

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.650
He ate our lunch!

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.110
Are you okay?!

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.500
M-My daughter is...!

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.830
That man is...!

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.000
That's...

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.100
a Grey Guard!

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.330
But, he's alone?

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.600
There might be others nearby.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.050
Lief, focus on rescuing that girl for now!

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.180
I know!

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.680
Stop!

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.690
Jasmine, take the girl now!

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.000
Come, let's hurry and get out of here!

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.620
Jill! What are you doing?! Run!

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.630
I am your opponent!

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.400
I was so close...

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.300
to making friends with her...

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.480
What are you talking about?

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.200
You've got it wrong. You've got it wrong!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:33.300
I just... wanted to give
these berries to that girl!

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.000
You deserted?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.170
That's correct.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.700
Just like all the rest, I was created to
serve the Shadow Lord in his army.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:58.500
I am number 6 in my pod.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.180
But...

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:08.190
unlike the other Grey Guards, I didn't
have the will to fight or even hurt humans.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:15.300
Rather, I find joy in making
friends with all sorts of creatures.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.800
It would appear that I'm a defective Grey Guard.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:27.200
As a failure, I was supposed
to be disposed of immediately...

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.100
But you managed to flee from the Shadowlands.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.100
This really is a surprise.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.000
I didn't think it was possible for there
to be a Grey Guard like yourself.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:48.000
Ah, please help yourself to these.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:49.600
Thank you.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.000
I'm not convinced.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.940
He's still a Grey Guard.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.800
The fact that he's our enemy hasn't changed.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.100
Come, Filli.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.200
It's as Ms. Jasmine says.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.130
It's true that I was created as a Grey Guard.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:17.130
The villagers are also afraid
of me and keep their distance.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.000
Uh...

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.700
Are you really sure about this...?

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.600
I'm sure that as long as we talk it out,

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.300
the villagers will come to see
that you're not a bad guy.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.800
But...

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.520
Don't worry about it.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:10.810
Go for it!

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.100
Ah... um,

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.600
hello.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.200
Here you go.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.400
Thank you!

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.600
See, didn't I tell you it would go well?

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.080
Mr. Lief, thank so much-

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.090
It's a Grey Guard!!

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.300
Oh no!

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:43.000
Run! The Grey Guards are coming!

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:44.900
You've got it wrong!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.800
Everyone, please listen!

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:47.600
He is...

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:48.310
Jill!!

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.500
Taking things from the
Grey Guards... Get rid of it!!

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.400
What is going on?!

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.200
Why doesn't anyone understand?

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.820
It's fine, Mr. Lief.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:04.100
I may be defective, but I'm still a Grey Guard.

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:07.300
If my mere presence scares the villagers,

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.830
I couldn't possibly get along with them...

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:21.100
You want to help Number 6
and the villagers to get along?

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:21.880
Yeah.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.500
Let's do what we can to help him.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.000
You can count me out.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:27.890
Jasmine...!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.100
That Grey Guard isn't a bad person.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.400
That's right.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.000
Even Filli and Kree were comfortable
around him, weren't they?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.400
I know that!

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.600
I know that...

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:43.400
But...

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.700
I'm begging you, Jasmine.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.120
We need your help no matter what.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.800
Fine.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.500
But I'm only going to help
because you're asking me to, Lief.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.880
I have no interest in helping him whatsoever.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.400
Thank you, Jasmine.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.100
But Lief,

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:06.470
just how do you plan on convincing
the villagers to accept him?

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:11.720
I have a good idea.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:19.300
This isn't quite how I imagined it...

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:23.800
I want something more... intense.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.000
I don't want to hear any complaints!

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.600
This my first time making something like this!

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:35.500
Alright! Then, let's go over
our plan one more time.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:41.100
First, Barda and I are going to dress up
as a monster and show up in the village.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:47.720
And while the villagers are being
frightened by this terrifying monster,

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.900
Number 6 will appear and bravely fight them off.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:57.100
And after saving the village from danger,

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:03.770
Number 6 will get along with the
villagers and live happily ever after.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.000
A perfect plan.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:13.900
Hey, come on... Do you seriously think
this childish trick will work?

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:15.400
It's fine.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:19.500
Where the costume is lacking, we will
make up for with our performance!

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.900
That's not what I meant...

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:31.430
Hey, I can't see anything ahead of me.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:39.400
From where I'm standing, you two don't
look anything like a 'terrifying monster'.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.400
I-I...

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:46.800
It's a monster!!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.000
Wow. Looks to me like he was well spooked!

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.900
Alright! Now Jasmine will go and get Number 6!

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.000
Fine...

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:11.000
It's a monster!

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.400
Ms. Jasmine!

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:27.650
What's the matter?

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:31.990
B-Bad news! A monster has appeared in the village!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.400
A...

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.990
A monster?!

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.170
That's right. A monster has appeared!

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:54.700
At this rate, the villagers will be in danger!

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.200
Uh...

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.500
Hurry up and go!

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:03.400
Please save them!

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:06.440
What about Mr. Lief and Mr. Barda...?

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:07.800
Huh?

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:12.440
Uh... um...

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.700
<i>Hold on, this wasn't mentioned in the plan!</i>

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:22.800
About that, u-uh....

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.630
Lief and Barda... had something else to do!

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.050
Look! Over there!

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.500
This is bad!

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:44.100
<i>That's right! The next line... next line...</i>

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:48.100
Now, hurry and repel that monster!

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:51.600
You're asking too much of me, but...

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:56.800
I may be imagining it, but that
girl seems to be laughing...

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:57.320
Huh?

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:00.950
Uh...

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:04.100
I'm sure it's because... yeah!

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.400
It's because that girl is still so young!

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:09.600
She doesn't understand
how terrifying monsters are!

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.500
Is that so?!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.500
I see,

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:18.000
that must be the reason why that
girl is the only one who likes me...

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.300
M-More importantly,

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:25.800
right now, you're the only one who can
fight off that monster and save the village!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.900
B-But...

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:31.610
I can't really handle something like this...

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:36.100
My god! You're so annoying!

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.900
M-Miss Jasmine...?!

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:40.800
Get off your butt and beat that thing up!

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:43.800
What kind of Grey Guard are you?!

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:56.500
Here, I'll give these to you, so please go home.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.400
Thank you!

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.700
Hey...

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:07.400
Just how long is it going to
take for Number 6 to come?

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:11.000
The villagers are locking
themselves in their houses.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.480
I can't keep this up much longer...

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.500
What is Jasmine doing...?

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.000
Number 6?

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.200
You damn monster, attacking our village!

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.400
We will exterminate you!

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:33.800
Let's get him, everyone!

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:35.500
Take this!

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.100
Ouch...!

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.000
H-Hey,

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:43.600
what should we do, Lief?
This wasn't part of the plan!

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:46.350
How should I know what to do... ouch...!

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.500
What the hell are you doing...?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:03.870
Number 6?

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.600
<i>Finally mustered up the courage, has he?</i>

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.800
You can't run anymore!

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.500
Give it up already, you damn monster!

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:20.000
Hey, what should we do?!

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.900
At this point we'd be better
off explaining ourselves...

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:24.200
We can't!

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:27.000
If the villagers were to find out about this,

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:31.000
Number 6 will lose his last
chance to make friends with them!

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:33.000
But, at this rate...

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:41.300
Huh...?

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.400
That guy is...

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.540
the Grey Guard!!

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.600
Number 6! You're finally here!

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:54.200
Good grief.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:55.800
I was getting tired of waiting.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:59.130
Now, shall we get this over and done with?

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.900
Number 6?

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:04.800
Hey, what's happening?

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:08.100
What are you doing?!

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:11.200
Hurry up and defeat that monster already!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.200
Even though it did nothing wrong...

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.400
Huh?

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:20.900
Purely on the basis of its frightening appearance,
to be throwing rocks at it like that...

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:23.360
It just isn't right!

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:25.500
What are you talking about?!

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.700
I cannot just stand by and watch this happen!

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.300
Why are you trying to <i>protect</i> the monster?!

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.830
If you do that, rather than becoming
friends with the villagers...

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:39.900
W-We have you outnumbered over here!

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:45.000
That's right! Let's beat that
Grey Guard, along with the monster!!

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:55.850
You bastards!!

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:02.500
You stand before one of the Grey Guards
under the Shadow Lord's command!

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.500
Do you think you will be
spared for standing against me?!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.870
Step forth if you wish to die!

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:18.710
Here...

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:27.200
Did you not hear what I just said?!

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:33.100
Jill!!

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:37.300
That man...

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:40.800
Is that Number 6's true self?

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.300
It can't be... that's just...

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:44.780
That's not it.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:44.780
Huh?

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.300
That's not it.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:49.030
He's...

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.790
Mr. Monster, you're safe now.

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.300
Number 6...

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.000
You...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.790
He was pretending to be
the bad guy for our sake...

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.600
Now, please run away while you have the chance!

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:41.200
What are you planning to do?

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.900
We have no choice but to tell him the truth.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:47.000
But, this will be tough...

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:51.090
Ms. Jasmine...?

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:56.000
And Mr. Lief and Mr. Barda too!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.140
Those outfits...

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:09.700
I'm sorry. We were trying to do whatever we
could to help you get along with the villagers.

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:12.280
Well, that was the plan at least.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:14.800
Rather than becoming your friends,

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:18.600
they're now more afraid of you than ever.

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.500
We're very sorry to have caused all this...

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:24.200
I need to apologise as well.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:26.500
I'm sorry, Number 6.

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:28.500
It's fine!

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.600
Please raise your heads!

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:35.300
I also must apologise for not
realising what was happening.

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:37.500
Honestly, it's very embarrassing.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:41.770
What are you going to do now?

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:49.200
The Shadow Lord and his forces have left this kingdom.

00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:56.450
But, I'm sure the people's fear of the
Grey Guards won't ever disappear.

00:19:57.200 --> 00:20:03.100
But, I think I'm going to try and befriend
them, without misleading them.

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:08.000
That way, I think they will come to
understand me for who I am.

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:11.480
It may take quite some time, though...

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.200
Yeah!

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:22.500
I have no way of knowing
when my body will vanish.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:31.980
But, it's for that very reason
that I must live life to the fullest!

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:36.400
You are no defect.

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:41.370
Well, you may be a failure as a Grey Guard...

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:46.600
But your heart is, without a doubt, a human one.

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:47.700
That's right!

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:50.700
You're no different from us!

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:54.400
Thank you, Ms. Jasmine,

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:57.470
Mr. Lief, Mr. Barda.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:10.150
It's no use. I can't find anything.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:15.210
I'm so hungry, I'm about to pass out...

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.600
Here they are!

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.910
And again, this is all we get...?

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:27.000
Jasmine, be sure to keep Filli at bay.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.600
We can't afford to have him eat it all again.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.100
Come to think of it,

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:35.380
I wonder if that guy is doing alright...

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:38.700
I hope things are going well for him.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:43.100
He'll be fine!

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:40.590
Bye-bye, thank you! The memories that we shared

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:45.680
are like a never-fading diamond

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:50.680
Non-stop, I'm not going to hit the brakes

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:55.730
I have to continue making this album

00:22:56.390 --> 00:23:01.070
Three springtimes have passed since then

00:23:01.070 --> 00:23:05.450
but I still remember you

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:11.870
In this ever-changing city landscape

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:16.250
I'm going out today, wearing a new pair of shoes

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:20.290
in search of tomorrow

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:24.800
In this corner of the world

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:30.550
it really is a miracle that we met each other

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:34.930
It's great to know that today and tomorrow

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:38.060
we will be seeing each other countless times

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:40.400
Thank you

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:45.030
Let's chase after our hopes and dreams

00:23:45.030 --> 00:23:50.820
and with a deep breath, say "good morning" to the sun

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:56.370
Our hearts feel the time passing by, so hold me tight

00:23:56.370 --> 00:24:00.170
and we can start running towards our next adventure

00:24:06.100 --> 00:24:07.200
What?!

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:09.500
We're going to look after Tom's Shop?

00:24:09.500 --> 00:24:11.580
Hey now, are you sure about this?

00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:14.200
The three of us are good at adventuring,

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:16.400
but we've never been shop assistants before!

00:24:16.400 --> 00:24:20.960
